-- title:
--   Galois-stable Vélu quotient descends to ℚ
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a Weierstrass curve over $\mathbb{Q}$, let $Q$ be a point of the affine model of the base change $W\otimes\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ (for a fixed algebraic closure $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of $\mathbb{Q}$), and let $p$ be a natural number. Assume $p$ is prime, $p \neq 2$, the additive order of $Q$ is exactly $p$, and for every $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra automorphism $\sigma$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ the point $\sigma \cdot Q$ lies in the subgroup of integer multiples of $Q$. The conclusion is that there is a Weierstrass curve $V_0$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ whose base change along $\mathbb{Q} \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is equal, coefficient by coefficient, to the Vélu quotient of $W \otimes \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ associated with the finite set $S \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}} \times \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of coordinate pairs of the points $k \cdot Q$ for $1 \le k \le (p-1)/2$ (natural-number division; the point at infinity contributing the pair $(0,0)$). Here the Vélu quotient is the Weierstrass curve with the same $a_1, a_2, a_3$ as $W \otimes \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, with $a_4$ replaced by $a_4 - 5\sum_{P \in S} t(P)$ and $a_6$ by $a_6 - b_2 \sum_{P \in S} t(P) - 7\sum_{P \in S} w(P)$, for the Vélu quantities $t$ and $w$ attached to a point.
--
--   This is the rationality (descent) half of Vélu's construction of the quotient isogeny: when the cyclic subgroup generated by $Q$ is stable under the absolute Galois group, the Vélu sums are Galois-invariant, so the quotient Weierstrass curve is already defined over $\mathbb{Q}$. It feeds [`WeierstrassCurve.exists_integral_veluQuotient_rescale_of_galois_stable`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.exists_integral_veluQuotient_rescale_of_galois_stable), where the descended model is further rescaled to an integral one.
-- source:
